  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is consistently 0.00 and historical price trends show mean reversion or downward momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward spikes in price (e.g., >70.00) by 5–10% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices (last 3–5 days) when sentiment is neutral (0.00) to capture potential rebound.",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is significantly higher than forecast, reduce next period’s forecast by 2–5% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "When sentiment is non-zero (e.g., 0.33), align forecast with sentiment direction — e.g., if sentiment > 0, slightly increase forecast; if < 0, decrease."
  ]
}
